Linux Patching Made Simple!
Keeping your Linux system secure & stable isn’t optional — it’s a must! 🔒✨
 Here’s your quick guide 👇
🔹 1. What is Linux patching?
 Updating your system with bug fixes, security upgrades, and performance improvements.

🔹 2. Why is it important?
 ✅ Fix vulnerabilities
 ✅ Improve stability
 ✅ Stay compliant

🔹 3. How do you patch Linux?
 👉 RHEL: yum update -y
 👉 Debian: apt update && apt upgrade -y

🔹 4. Security patch vs Kernel patch
 🛡️ Security patch → Fixes vulnerabilities
 ⚡ Kernel patch → Boosts performance & adds new features

🔹 5. Rollback if things break?
 No stress 😎
 👉 yum history undo <id>
 👉 dpkg --remove <pkg> & reinstall older version

🔹 6. Live Patching = No Reboot 🎉
 Use tools like kpatch, ksplice, or Canonical Livepatch to update kernels without downtime.

💡 Pro tip: Consistent patching = less stress, more uptime 🚀
